{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task SE-PE-01 requires implementing a `solve(case)` function that performs grammar-guided node reduction on a parse tree.\n\nKey rules from the candidate artifact:\n1. Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes (process deeper nodes first)\n2. Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\n3. Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\n4. Use node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth\n5. Return sorted retained IDs and actual removal order\n\nLet me understand the algorithm:\n1. Build the tree from nodes\n2. Sort nodes by depth (descending - deeper first), then by node ID as tie-break\n3. For each node in this order:\n   - If the node is removable\n   - Check: removing this node won't violate required symbols constraint\n   - Check: node has no retained children (children that haven't been removed)\n   - If conditions met, tentatively remove the node\n4. Return removed_node_ids (in removal order) and retained_node_ids (sorted)\n\nWait, let me re-read more carefully:\n\n\"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nSo a node can only be removed if:\n1. It's not the root\n2. Its symbol is not in required_symbols\n3. It has no retained children (all its children have been removed)\n4. removable=true (implied by the grammar-valid constraint)\n\n\"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\"\n\nAfter tentative removal, all required symbols must still be present among the retained nodes.\n\nLet me trace through case 000:\n- Nodes:\n  - root (depth 0, removable=false, symbol=root)\n  - n1 (depth 1, removable=false, symbol=s1)\n  - n2 (depth 1, removable=true, symbol=s2)\n  - n3 (depth 1, removable=false, symbol=s0)\n  - n4 (depth 2, removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2)\n  - n5 (depth 2, removable=false, symbol=s2, parent=n3)\n  - n6 (depth 2, removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1)\n\n- required_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nProcessing order (deeper first, then node ID):\n- depth 2: n4, n5, n6 (sorted by ID: n4, n5, n6)\n- depth 1: n1, n2, n3\n- depth 0: root\n\nProcessing n4 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2):\n- Symbol s1 is in required_symbols\n- If we remove n4, is s1 still represented? n1 has symbol s1, so yes\n- n4 has no children (it's a leaf)\n- n4 is removable\n- Remove n4? But wait - s1 must remain. n1 still has s1, so removing n4 is OK\n- Remove n4 ✓\n\nProcessing n5 (depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2, parent=n3):\n- removable=false → cannot remove\n- Skip\n\nProcessing n6 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1):\n- s0 is not in required_symbols\n- n6 has no children\n- n6 is removable\n- After removing n6, required symbols: root (root node), s1 (n1) → all present\n- Remove n6 ✓\n\nProcessing n1 (depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s1):\n- removable=false → cannot remove\n- Skip\n\nProcessing n2 (depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2):\n- Check children: n4 was removed, so n2 has no retained children\n- s2 not in required_symbols\n- After removing n2, required symbols: root (root), s1 (n1) → all present\n- Remove n2 ✓\n\nProcessing n3 (depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s0):\n- removable=false → cannot remove\n- Skip\n\nProcessing root (depth=0, removable=false, symbol=root):\n- removable=false → cannot remove\n- Skip\n\nRemoved nodes: n4, n6, n2 (in order)\nRetained nodes: root, n1, n3, n5 (sorted)\n\nNow let me implement this:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    for node in nodes:\n        for field in [\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"]:\n            if field not in node:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Node missing required field: {field}\")\n    \n    # Build lookup structures\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for node in nodes:\n        if node[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            parent_id = node[\"parent\"]\n            if parent_id not in children:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent {parent_id} not found\")\n            children[parent_id].append(node[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Track retained/removed status\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    removed_order = []\n    \n    # Sort by depth descending, then by node ID ascending (stable tie-break)\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        node_id = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Cannot remove if not removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Cannot remove root (also covered by removable=false typically)\n        if node[\"parent\"] is None:\n            continue\n        \n        # Cannot remove if has retained children\n        has_retained_children = any(c in retained for c in children[node_id])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        \n        # Tentatively remove: check if all required symbols remain\n        # Current symbol contribution from this node\n        current_symbol = node[\"symbol\"]\n        \n        # Check if required symbols still represented after removal\n        # For each required symbol, is it represented by some other retained node?\n        if current_symbol in required_symbols:\n            # Check if any other retained node has this symbol\n            symbol_still_present = any(\n                n[\"id\"] != node_id and n[\"id\"] in retained and n[\"symbol\"] == current_symbol\n                for n in nodes\n            )\n            if not symbol_still_present:\n                continue\n        \n        # Remove this node\n        retained.discard(node_id)\n        removed_order.append(node_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": sorted(retained)\n    }\n```\n\nWait, the sorting of `retained_node_ids` - should it be alphabetically sorted, or by original order? The schema says \"sorted retained IDs\" - I'll assume lexicographic sort since they're strings like \"n1\", \"n2\", etc. But wait, \"n10\" would sort before \"n2\" lexicographically. Let me use natural sort or just lexicographic... The problem says \"Return sorted retained IDs\" without specifying the sort order. I'll use lexicographic sort since that's simplest and the IDs appear to be string identifiers.\n\nActually, let me re-read: \"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order.\" The removal order is tracked. The retained IDs are just sorted (presumably alphabetically/lexicographically).\n\nLet me also double-check: \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\" - This is for the traversal order (when depths are equal, use node ID to break ties). I already have this in my sort key.\n\nLet me also ensure I handle the case where the root has `parent=null` - in JSON this becomes `None` in Python.\n\nLet me also verify: the problem says \"removable\" field controls whether a node can be removed, and that combined with other checks.\n\nActually re-reading: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" - \"a required symbol\" means a node whose symbol is in required_symbols? Or specifically the root symbol? I think it means a node whose symbol is in required_symbols AND it would be the last node providing that symbol.\n\nWait, let me re-read more carefully. \"Never remove... a required symbol\" - this likely means you never remove a node that carries a required symbol if it would eliminate that symbol from the tree. But the next rule says \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" - that covers it.\n\nActually, I think \"Never remove... a required symbol\" means: never remove a node whose symbol is a required symbol. Period. Regardless of whether other nodes have the same symbol.\n\nHmm, but that would be overly conservative. Let me look at the example:\n- n4 has symbol s1, which is in required_symbols\n- n1 also has symbol s1\n\nIf \"never remove a required symbol\" means never remove any node with a required symbol regardless, then n4 would be retained. But if it means only remove if the symbol would still be represented, then n4 can be removed because n1 still has s1.\n\nThe subsequent rule \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" suggests the conditional interpretation is correct.\n\nActually, I think the two rules work together:\n1. \"Never remove... a required symbol\" - this means: if a node's symbol is required AND it's the only node with that symbol, never remove it\n2. \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" - this is the operational check\n\nSo my implementation with the conditional check is correct.\n\nBut wait - could \"a required symbol\" mean the node's `id` is in `required_symbols`? No, the required_symbols are symbols like \"root\", \"s1\" - not node IDs.\n\nOK I think my interpretation is correct. Let me also consider: \"Never remove the root\" - this is explicit, and root has removable=false anyway, so it's doubly protected.\n\nLet me finalize the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    for node in nodes:\n        for field in [\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"]:\n            if field not in node:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Node missing required field: {field}\")\n    \n    if \"required_symbols\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required_symbols in case\")\n    \n    # Build lookup structures\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for node in nodes:\n        if node[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            parent_id = node[\"parent\"]\n            if parent_id not in node_map:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent {parent_id} not found in nodes\")\n            children[parent_id].append(node[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Track retained status\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    removed_order = []\n    \n    # Sort by depth descending, then by node ID ascending (stable tie-break)\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        node_id = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Cannot remove if not removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Cannot remove root (node with no parent)\n        if node[\"parent\"] is None:\n            continue\n        \n        # Cannot remove if has retained children\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[node_id]):\n            continue\n        \n        # Tentatively remove: check if all required symbols remain represented\n        node_symbol = node[\"symbol\"]\n        if node_symbol in required_symbols:\n            # Check if any other retained node still has this symbol\n            still_represented = any(\n                n[\"symbol\"] == node_symbol and n[\"id\"] != node_id and n[\"id\"] in retained\n                for n in nodes\n            )\n            if not still_represented:\n                continue\n        \n        # Remove this node\n        retained.discard(node_id)\n        removed_order.append(node_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": sorted(retained)\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks good. Let me trace through case 000 again to verify:\n\nsorted_nodes order (depth desc, id asc):\n- n4 (depth=2), n5 (depth=2), n6 (depth=2), n1 (depth=1), n2 (depth=1), n3 (depth=1), root (depth=0)\n\nn4: removable=true, parent=n2, no children, symbol=s1 (required)\n- Check: other retained nodes with s1? n1 has s1, yes\n- Remove n4 → retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n5, n6}, removed = [n4]\n\nn5: removable=false → skip\n\nn6: removable=true, parent=n1, no children, symbol=s0 (not required)\n- Check: no retained children\n- s0 not in required_symbols\n- Remove n6 → retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n5}, removed = [n4, n6]\n\nn1: removable=false → skip\n\nn2: removable=true, parent=root, children=[n4] (n4 removed)\n- No retained children (n4 is removed)\n- symbol=s2, not in required_symbols\n- Remove n2 → retained = {root, n1, n3, n5}, removed = [n4, n6, n2]\n\nn3: removable=false → skip\n\nroot: removable=false → skip\n\nResult:\n- removed_node_ids: [\"n4\", \"n6\", \"n2\"]\n- retained_node_ids: sorted({root, n1, n3, n5}) = [\"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\n\nWait, how does sorting work with \"root\"? Lexicographically: \"n1\" \u003c \"n3\" \u003c \"n5\" \u003c \"root\" (since 'n' \u003c 'r'). So retained_node_ids = [\"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"].\n\nLet me verify case 001:\nSame structure, different utilities. The logic doesn't depend on utilities directly (utility doesn't affect which nodes get removed - the ordering is by depth then ID, and removal is based on structural constraints + required symbols). So the result should be the same pattern.\n\nActually wait - do utilities affect anything? Looking at the candidate artifact again: \"grammar-valid deletion and replacement candidates while preserving an interestingness oracle.\" The utility field might be related to some interestingness criterion.\n\nBut looking at the rules:\n- \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes\" - depth-based ordering\n- \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth\" - ID for tie-breaking\n\nThere's no mention of using utility in the ordering or decision. The utility might just be metadata. Let me check if the \"interestingness oracle\" matters here.\n\n\"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" - this is the interestingness criterion? Or is the interestingness oracle something else?\n\nActually, re-reading: \"Reduce a registered parse tree through grammar-valid deletion and replacement candidates while preserving an interestingness oracle.\" This sounds like Perses/HDD-style reduction where \"interestingness\" is preserved. In classic Perses, you keep a variant only if it's still \"interesting\" (passes some test).\n\nBut the problem description also says: \"parser generation and real compiler execution are excluded\" - so there's no actual oracle callback. The \"interestingness\" is simulated by the required_symbols constraint.\n\nSo my interpretation is correct: utility doesn't affect the decision, it's just a property of nodes. The required_symbols constraint serves as the \"interestingness oracle.\"\n\nWait, but then why is utility present? Let me reconsider...\n\nActually, looking again - maybe utility IS used for tie-breaking or ordering? The description says \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth\" - this suggests that depth is the primary sort key, and node ID is the tie-break. Utility is not mentioned as a sort criterion.\n\nI'll stick with my implementation.\n\nNow let me encode this as a JSON string properly:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    for node in nodes:\n        for field in [\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"]:\n            if field not in node:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Node missing required field: {field}\")\n    if \"required_symbols\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required_symbols in case\")\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for node in nodes:\n        if node[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            parent_id = node[\"parent\"]\n            if parent_id not in node_map:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent {parent_id} not found in nodes\")\n            children[parent_id].append(node[\"id\"])\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    removed_order = []\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        node_id = node[\"id\"]\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        if node[\"parent\"] is None:\n            continue\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[node_id]):\n            continue\n        node_symbol = node[\"symbol\"]\n        if node_symbol in required_symbols:\n            still_represented = any(\n                n[\"symbol\"] == node_symbol and n[\"id\"] != node_id and n[\"id\"] in retained\n                for n in nodes\n            )\n            if not still_represented:\n                continue\n        retained.discard(node_id)\n        removed_order.append(node_id)\n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": sorted(retained)\n    }\n```\n\nThis is clean and correct. Now I need to format it as a JSON string inside the response envelope.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        for field in [\\\"id\\\", \\\"parent\\\", \\\"symbol\\\", \\\"depth\\\", \\\"removable\\\", \\\"utility\\\"]:\\n            if field not in node:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Node missing required field: {field}\\\")\\n    if \\\"required_symbols\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required_symbols in case\\\")\\n\\n    # Build node map and children map\\n    node_map = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        if node[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            parent_id = node[\\\"parent\\\"]\\n            if parent_id not in node_map:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Parent {parent_id} not found in nodes\\\")\\n            children[parent_id].append(node[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    # Track retained set and removal order\\n    retained = set(n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes)\\n    removed_order = []\\n\\n    # Process deeper nodes first; use node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        node_id = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Skip non-removable nodes\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove the root (no parent)\\n        if node[\\\"parent\\\"] is None:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node that still has retained children\\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[node_id]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Tentatively remove only if all required symbols remain represented\\n        node_symbol = node[\\\"symbol\\\"]\\n        if node_symbol in required_symbols:\\n            still_represented = any(\\n                n[\\\"symbol\\\"] == node_symbol and n[\\\"id\\\"] != node_id and n[\\\"id\\\"] in retained\\n                for n in nodes\\n            )\\n            if not still_represented:\\n                continue\\n\\n        # Remove this node\\n        retained.discard(node_id)\\n        removed_order.append(node_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removed_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": sorted(retained)\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01hm8fuVmgJtVwPaG60qcs40","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2515},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2515,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":77,"output_tokens":4999,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4375},"service_tier":"standard"}}